			<div class="content" id="post-content-1621985">
									

<p>*shrug* I find all three activities entertaining, depending on my mood, so it's all good.</p>
<p>It all boils down to the same basic questions that fueled the Terry Schiavo controvery. What is &quot;alive&quot;, what is &quot;dead&quot;, what is the minimum that can be left from a collection of bodily functions to be considered the &quot;same person&quot;? Certainly larger questions than we'll ever figure out on a horror fiction wiki.</p>
<p>It would be a harder challenge if the terms were tighter. Possibly not a better one, but definitely harder; like I said up top, I liked this story. Metaphysical debate is just icing.</p>

