														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1622206">
									

<p>The problem is that both sides of that particular battle (and similar ones in general) have deep emotional investment which are both valid, but lead to radically different viewpoints/outcomes. And once someone's emotions become involved in the debate, <em>especially</em> when they're that strong, it's next to impossible for <em>ANYONE</em> to &quot;win&quot; the argument. Attempts to get someone to see it your way get interpreted as &quot;you're saying my emotions aren't valid&quot; and cause the other person to just entrench further in their belief/viewpoint. Everyone does it to one degree or another, whether they intend to or not.</p>
<p>But that's neither here nor there, and this kind of debate doesn't really belong here. If you're interested in continuing the discussion, feel free to PM me.</p>

