				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/drewbear" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(301632); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=301632&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608887573" alt="Drewbear" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=301632)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/drewbear" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(301632); return false;" >Drewbear</a></span> <span class="odate time_1353510369 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">21 Nov 2012 15:06</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1623101">
									

<p>As for your concern that the &quot;self-hating faggot&quot; cliche, well, it's a cliche for a <em>reason</em>. There were a lot of men in that era who felt that way, and to a degree, still are today. Keep in mind that back then, the only real mainstream concept of homosexual men was the stereotypical lisping, un-manly faggot, and because of that, any man that WASN'T that, but still had sexual feelings for men, had a <em>STRONG</em> tendency to self-denial/deception/hatred. Hell, a lot of 'em were probably actually bisexual, but that possibility wasn't even KNOWN to the general culture; if you wanted to have sex with a man, EVER, even if only one time, even if you liked having sex with women, that made you a faggot.</p>

							</div>

										<div class="signature">
					<hr class="signature-separator"/>
					

<p>Giving bearhugs to the unsuspecting since 1872.</p>

				</div>
					
					
